{title: 469 - Leaning on the Everlasting Arms}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #469 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 469}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Ab]What a fellowship, [Bbm]what a [Db]joy divine,
[Ab]Leaning on the everlasting [Eb]arms;
[Ab]What a blessedness, [Bbm]what a [Db]peace is mine,
[Ab]Leaning on the ever[Eb7]lasting [Ab]arms.
[Ab]Leaning, [Db]leaning, [Ab]Safe and secure [Eb]from [Ab]all a[Eb]larms;
[Ab]Leaning, [Db]leaning, [Ab]Leaning on the ever[Eb7]lasting [Ab]arms.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Ab][Bbm]Leaning, [Db]leaning,
[Ab]safe and secure [Eb]from all alarms;
[Ab][Bbm]leaning, [Db]leaning,
[Ab]leaning [Eb7]on the [Ab]everlasting arms.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Ab]O how sweet [Bbm]to walk in [Db]this pilgrim way,
[Ab]leaning on [Eb]the everlasting arms;
[Ab]O how bright [Bbm]the path grows [Db]from day to day,
[Ab]leaning [Eb7]on the [Ab]everlasting arms.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Ab]What have I [Bbm]to dread, what [Db]have I to fear,
[Ab]leaning on [Eb]the everlasting arms?
[Ab]I have blessed [Bbm]peace with my [Db]Lord so near,
[Ab]leaning [Eb7]on the [Ab]everlasting arms.
{end_of_verse}
